<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Banco Rio to be listed in September.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Banco Rio to be listed in September.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Banco Rio de la Plata is to be stock listed in the United States and in Europe at the end of September, state news agency Telam reported Monday.</p>
<p>Spanish bank Santander bought a controlling stake in Banco Rio for $594 million in May, at which time it stated its intention to list the Argentine bank.</p>
<p>Santander will manage the stock issue in Europe and Merrill Lynch will be in charge in the United States, Telam said, quoting Banco Rio officials.</p>
<p>The equity issue will take place through a &quot;book building&quot; system.</p>
<p>((--Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668)).</p>
